  "body": "## Summary\n\nBase `focus-without-user-activation` authorization on the document initiating the focus change,\nrather than the document receiving focus.\n\nThis separates two questions: whether a document may initiate a focus move, and whether the\ndestination is valid for focusing. Script entry points capture the incumbent global's associated\ndocument and pass it explicitly through the dialog and popover algorithms. Declarative\ninvocations use the invoker's document and autofocus uses the element's document.\n\nRelated: whatwg/html#12032, whatwg/html#12470, and whatwg/html#11839.\n\n## Motivation\n\nAn allowed parent should be able to delegate focus into a child with the feature denied. Conversely,\na restricted initiator should not be authorized just because its target has the feature enabled,\nhas transient activation, or already has focus.\n\nOnce an embedded application receives focus, it also needs to manage its controls, delegate to nested\ncontent, and reclaim focus from that content. These are the compatibility cases described in whatwg/html#11839.\n\nThe [TPAC 2024 resolution](https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-permissions-policy/issues/273#issuecomment-2384287101) requires parent to child delegation.\n\n## Allow focus steps\n\n```text\nallow focus steps(focusSetterDocument):\n  1. If focusSetterDocument is not fully active, return false.\n  2. If focusSetterDocument is allowed to use focus-without-user-activation policy, return true.\n  3. If focusSetterDocument's relevant global has transient activation, return true.\n  4. Return has focus steps(focusSetterDocument).\n```\n\nThe target's policy and activation no longer grant permission.\n\n`has focus steps` includes focus in descendant navigables and requires the top-level traversable to\nhave system focus. A restricted document can therefore manage focus while it or one of its\ndescendants has focus.\n\n## Intended behavior\n\nLet allowed document A contain restricted B and D, with restricted C nested inside B. Unless noted,\nthere is no transient activation.\n\n| Scenario | Result |\n|---|---|\n| A focuses an element in restricted B | Allow: A's policy authorizes it |\n| Focused B focuses another element in B | Allow |\n| Focused B delegates to child C | Allow |\n| C is focused; B retakes focus into its own document | Allow |\n| Focused B hands focus to sibling D or back to A | Allow |\n| Focus has moved to D; B tries to reclaim it without activation | Deny |\n| Unfocused B targets allowed A | Deny: A's policy does not authorize B |\n| Only D has activation; B tries to focus D | Deny: D's activation does not authorize B |\n| Unfocused D targets B while focus is in B's child C | Deny |\n| B has transient activation and requests focus outside its subtree | Allow |\n\nAn allowed or already focused initiator may request focus across an opener/popup relationship, subject\nto existing access and focusing rules, this does not override restrictions on system level window focus. \nA restricted popup with neither transient activation nor focus in its subtree fails the permission check\neven if its opener has the feature enabled.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11519/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Sep 24, 2026, 6:36 PM UTC (59670dd)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11519/6a6ee7a...59670dd/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Sep 24, 2026, 6:36 PM UTC (59670dd)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11519/form-elements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Sep 24, 2026, 6:36 PM UTC (59670dd)\">/form-elements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11519/6a6ee7a...59670dd/form-elements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Sep 24, 2026, 6:36 PM UTC (59670dd)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11519/interaction.html\" title=\"Last updated on Sep 24, 2026, 6:36 PM UTC (59670dd)\">/interaction.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11519/6a6ee7a...59670dd/interaction.html\" title=\"Last updated on Sep 24, 2026, 6:36 PM UTC (59670dd)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11519/interactive-elements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Sep 24, 2026, 6:36 PM UTC (59670dd)\">/interactive-elements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11519/6a6ee7a...59670dd/interactive-elements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Sep 24, 2026, 6:36 PM UTC (59670dd)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11519/popover.html\" title=\"Last updated on Sep 24, 2026, 6:36 PM UTC (59670dd)\">/popover.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11519/6a6ee7a...59670dd/popover.html\" title=\"Last updated on Sep 24, 2026, 6:36 PM UTC (59670dd)\">diff</a> )",
